<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The sweep, the ablation and the wavelength bracket sit next to the Lean theorems for the discriminant, the equal-diffusivity failure and the 36-37x ratio against the 24 µm sibling. The composite path is now one signed resample. The integer Jacobian in Lean is the Schnakenberg state cleared by 5, which the script comments and does not re-derive in Lean." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the pseudo-spectral Schnakenberg step and the eigenvalue comparison, and now checks the two classical corollaries: the band disappears when Du = Dv, and the selected wavelength lengthens as Dv/Du increases above threshold. Kinetics remain a minimal carrier, not a cavefish-derived pair, which is why the score stays short of the top of the scale." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph — Morphometric validation: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pearson r = 0.99997 and RMSE = 0.00455 on 11 modes. Nonlinear wavelength 660.7 nm versus the 665.6 nm linear calibration. Ablation sigma_max = -0.1 against a marginal reference of 0. Flank orientation KS = 0.105 (not 0). Melanin-dark fraction on the body mask is 0.002 against the Oca2-null reference of 0. The KS samples orientations with a fixed seed; it is not a spatial registration of melanophores." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
