<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 666 nm in the Astyanax cave morph — MorphoEval overall 85.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2. Same Schnakenberg carrier and 6.656e-7 m calibration as pass 1 (Holocene cave morph, 0 Ma). Dispersion Pearson r remains 0.99997 (RMSE 0.00455). Nonlinear wavelength 660.7 nm. The Dv/Du sweep on {10, 12, 16, 20, 24, 30} is monotonic: selected wavelength rises from 15.74 px to 19.88 px. Du = Dv = 2 suppresses the band (sigma_max = -0.1). The voucher flank and the patch differ by KS = 0.105 on magnitude-weighted Sobel orientations (p about 1e-24). The unused resample buffer in the composite is gone. Eye loss and neuromast expansion are still outside k_c. Overall 85.1/100 (faithfulness 84.1, reproducibility 87.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 88, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/astyanax_mexicanus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 527335 B, 1232×880 px, artifact_sha256 8f2c47046806390ff06fb6e96b06695196831a98801af737309e72b78e2c0e74 (sha256 8f2c47046806390ff06fb6e96b06695196831a98801af737309e72b78e2c0e74), spec_fingerprint 567daaa26ea32b6e0db869c7c7df6b1cf14d5ac54c7e7b02f34d577ba1dab69a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 567daaa26ea32b6e0db869c7c7df6b1cf14d5ac54c7e7b02f34d577ba1dab69a; artifact_sha256: 8f2c47046806390ff06fb6e96b06695196831a98801af737309e72b78e2c0e74; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/astyanax_mexicanus_turing_wavelength_s0/astyanax_mexicanus_specimen.jpg=b7b2d7744b19592f..., datasets/astyanax_mexicanus_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=a4f57d067c37118a...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952), Schnakenberg (1979) and Murray (1981) supply the instability, the kinetics and the coat-marking wavelength idea. | oca2 and mc1r, not a measured 666 nm mode, account for cavefish pigment loss (Protas et al. 2006; Gross et al. 2009; McCauley, Hixon and Jeffery 2004). | Yamamoto, Stock and Jeffery (2004) and Yoshizawa et al. (2010) are the sources for eye degeneration and neuromast expansion. Neither is a Turing-wavelength result.; reconstructed_in_script: Metres per pixel are set so the fastest linear mode equals 6.656e-7 m. That length is the loop card, not a cavefish measurement. | Pass 2 adds a six-point diffusion-ratio sweep, an equal-diffusivity ablation, and a flank-versus-patch KS statistic. Pearson r, RMSE and the 660.7 nm nonlinear peak are unchanged from pass 1.; transfer_boundary: The GIF still composites a subcellular patch onto a whole-body photograph. High computer-vision similarity is dominated by the shared silhouette. It does not show that the camera resolved 666 nm.; does_not_claim: Does not claim optic-cup degeneration or neuromast expansion are produced by k_c. | Does not claim Schnakenberg parameters were identified in Astyanax tissue. | Does not claim a fossil predecessor. The chronoseries is the single extant cave morph at 0 Ma. The 24 µm sibling is a scale comparison, ratio 36.33.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'The 666 nm length is imposed by the slot card. A wet-lab measurement of melanosome spacing on this species would replace the metres-per-pixel calibration.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R6', 'item': 'No nanopub profile was present, so pass 2 is not signed. Signing waits on ~/.nanopub/profile.yml.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.51e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-astyanax-mexicanus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
